Switzerland does not recognise Polish qualified signatures under an eIDAS-equivalent framework: no mutual recognition agreement exists between Switzerland and the EU, and without one a foreign qualified signature is not equivalent to a qualified signature under Swiss law ([BAKOM](https://www.bakom.admin.ch/en/electronic-signature)). CERT Polska states the impact as remote code execution from combining a genuine signed JAR with a malicious ZIP, in all SzafirHost versions before 1.2.1 ([CERT Polska, 2026-05-15](https://cert.pl/en/posts/2026/05/CVE-2026-44088/)); it describes no attack on the download path, no silent signing of fraudulent documents and no list of public-sector workflows that depend on the helper, so those statements are withdrawn. The CVSS 4.0 base score of 8.6 is CERT-PL's as the numbering authority, carried by ENISA's EUVD ([ENISA EUVD-2026-30512](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/enisa/eu_vulnerability_database/EUVD-2026-30512)).
